  <h2>Research Interests</h2>
<p>
  My research interests lie in developing mathematical and statistical methods for biomedical
  data, with a focus on spatial structure and cellular heterogeneity. My work includes spatial
  and topological analysis of histopathology images and analysis of paired single-cell gene
  expression and chromatin accessibility data.
</p>
<p>
  I am a senior at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, pursuing a double major in Mathematics
  and Statistics &amp; Analytics. I work with Dr. Fuhai Li at Washington University School of
  Medicine as a visiting researcher. At UNC, I am a senior honors thesis candidate advised by
  Dr. Zoe Huang, currently undertaking directed reading on Markov chain mixing times and cutoff phenomena.
</p>
